# Answer key for B3 t4_adversarial.sql - DML-specific traps.
#
# WRITTEN FROM SOURCE BEFORE THE ANALYSER WAS RUN OVER THIS FILE.
# The forbidden list is the test. Conventions: B1/B2 plus D-15..D-18 (not implemented).

@ 20 S1 a target alias spelled like another table
value core.dim_store.country_code -> core.dim_store.region identity
filter staging.customers.status -> core.dim_store
forbid value staging.customers.country_code -> core.dim_store.region | `customers` in the SET is the TARGET alias (dim_store); staging.customers is `c`
forbid filter staging.customers.country_code -> core.dim_store | `c.country_code = customers.country_code` joins the FROM list to the target (D-11)

@ 30 S2 EXCLUDED is the proposed row
value staging.customers.id -> mart.customer_summary.customer_id identity
value staging.customers.country_code -> mart.customer_summary.segment identity
forbid value staging.customers.segment -> mart.customer_summary.segment | EXCLUDED.segment is the value PROPOSED for segment - x.country_code - not the source's own segment column

@ 40 S3 the target joined to itself
value core.dim_customer.first_order_date -> core.dim_customer.first_order_date identity
filter core.dim_customer.is_current -> core.dim_customer
forbid filter core.dim_customer.customer_id -> core.dim_customer | the self-join key joins FROM to the target (D-11)

@ 52 S4 two SETs reading each other's OLD values
value core.dim_product.cost -> core.dim_product.list_price derived
value core.dim_product.list_price -> core.dim_product.cost identity
forbid value core.dim_product.cost -> core.dim_product.cost | every SET reads the OLD row: cost gets the old list_price, not the new `cost * 2`

@ 61 S5 an explicit column list out of table order
value staging.customers.full_name -> mart.top_customers.full_name identity
value staging.customers.id -> mart.top_customers.customer_id identity
value staging.customers.country_code -> mart.top_customers.region identity
forbid value staging.customers.full_name -> mart.top_customers.region | an explicit column list binds by ITS order, not the table's

@ 70 S6 an omitted column list, fewer values than columns
value staging.orders.order_ts -> mart.channel_mix.period_month derived
value staging.orders.channel -> mart.channel_mix.channel identity
forbid value staging.orders.channel -> mart.channel_mix.region | the omitted list binds to the FIRST columns in table order

@ 78 S7 RETURNING an expression from a DELETE (D-16)
value core.fct_shipment.cost -> <result>.doubled_cost derived
value core.fct_shipment.shipment_id -> <result>.shipment_id identity
filter core.fct_shipment.status -> core.fct_shipment
filter core.fct_shipment.status -> <result>

@ 87 S8 MERGE whose USING alias is the target's name
value core.dim_store.name -> core.dim_warehouse.name identity
forbid value core.dim_warehouse.name -> core.dim_warehouse.name | `dim_warehouse` here is the USING alias for core.dim_store

@ 98 S9 a correlated subquery in an UPDATE's WHERE
filter core.fct_order_line.product_key, core.dim_product.product_key -> core.dim_product
filter core.fct_order_line.quantity -> core.dim_product post
forbid value core.fct_order_line.quantity -> core.dim_product.status | the subquery is in WHERE: it decides which rows are updated; D-18 is about SET

@ 108 S10a a writable CTE read by a bare SELECT
filter staging.web_events.event_ts -> staging.web_events
filter staging.web_events.event_ts -> <result>
note `removed` is COUNT(*): no value source. D-17: the predicate decides what is deleted and what is counted.

@ 122 S10b a writable CTE nothing reads
filter staging.inventory_snapshots.on_hand -> staging.inventory_snapshots
note PostgreSQL executes it regardless; losing this is losing a write silently.

@ 134 S11 ON CONFLICT ON CONSTRAINT, DO UPDATE WHERE on EXCLUDED
value staging.inventory_snapshots.snapshot_date -> mart.sales_daily.sale_date identity
value staging.inventory_snapshots.warehouse_id -> mart.sales_daily.store_id identity
value staging.inventory_snapshots.on_hand -> mart.sales_daily.units identity
filter staging.inventory_snapshots.on_hand -> mart.sales_daily
forbid filter staging.inventory_snapshots.snapshot_date -> mart.sales_daily | sales_daily_uk's columns are the conflict target: structural (D-15)
